  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ITP 322 Social protection - ITP Social protection EPRI</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">ITP 322 Social trygghet</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Den f&#xf6;reslagna insatsen &#xe4;r ett globalt kapacitetsutvecklingsprogram inom sociala trygghetssystem. Implementerande parter &#xe4;r Economic Policy Research Institute (EPRI); ett Sydafrika-baserat forskningsinstitut, i samarbete med Arbetsf&#xf6;rmedlingen (AF). Inom ramen f&#xf6;r insatsen koordinerar AF medverkan fr&#xe5;n andra svenska expertmyndigheter relevanta inom omr&#xe5;det social trygghet (s&#xe5; som Pensionsmyndigheten, F&#xf6;rs&#xe4;kringskassan och Skatteverket). 

Syftet med den f&#xf6;reslagna ITP:n &#xe4;r att bidra till f&#xf6;rb&#xe4;ttrade sociala trygghetssystem f&#xf6;r f&#xf6;rst&#xe4;rkt fattigdomsbek&#xe4;mpning, minskad s&#xe5;rbarhet, mindre oj&#xe4;mlikhet (g&#xe4;llande s&#xe5;v&#xe4;l k&#xf6;nsskillnader som ekonomisk oj&#xe4;mlikhet) samt att motverka social utslagning och bidra till inkluderande social utveckling och r&#xe4;ttvis ekonomisk tillv&#xe4;xt. Programmet kommer att genomf&#xf6;ras i tio till femton l&#xe4;nder i Afrika och Asien. Den f&#xf6;rsta pilotomg&#xe5;ngen genomf&#xf6;rs i Etiopien, Kenya, Tanzania, Uganda och Zambia.

Avsedda resultat inkluderar:
1) St&#xe4;rkt kapacitet hos offentliga institutioner 
2) F&#xf6;rb&#xe4;ttrade sociala trygghetssystem/resultat
3) bidra till utvecklingssynergier
4) Bidra till ett r&#xe4;ttighetsbaserat arbetss&#xe4;tt som st&#xe4;rker j&#xe4;mst&#xe4;lldhet mellan k&#xf6;nen
5) F&#xf6;rst&#xe4;rkning av organisatorisk integritet

K&#xe4;rnmodulerna i ITP kommer att omfatta kapacitetsutveckling inom sex huvudomr&#xe5;den:
1) Ramverk f&#xf6;r sociala trygghetssystem som &#xe4;r r&#xe4;ttighetsbaserade och inkluderar hela livscykeln
2) Utformning och genomf&#xf6;rande av sociala trygghetssystem f&#xf6;r att s&#xe4;kerst&#xe4;lla social inkludering  
3) St&#xe4;rka utvecklingseffekterna (social protection plus och SDGs)
4) St&#xe4;rkt integrering av j&#xe4;mst&#xe4;lldhetsperspektivet i sociala trygghetssystem
5) Finansiering och samfinansiering av reformer, utvidgning och koordinering av sociala trygghetssystem
6) F&#xf6;lja upp och utv&#xe4;rdera sociala trygghetssystem f&#xf6;r att m&#xf6;jligg&#xf6;ra evidensbaserad f&#xf6;r&#xe4;ndring.

 ITP:n kommer dessutom att utveckla specifika moduler och komponenter f&#xf6;r att st&#xf6;dja de specifika f&#xf6;r&#xe4;ndringsprojekt som identifieras av landteamen.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The proposed intervention is an international training programme (ITP) on social protection, to be implemented in 2019-2023.  Implementing partners are Economic Policy Research Institute (EPRI); a  South-Africa based research institute, in collaboration with the Swedish Public Employment Service (AF). In this programme, AF is also coordinating the contribution of other Swedish expert authorities relevant in the area of social protection (Swedish Pensions Agency, The Swedish Social Insurance Agency, The Swedish Tax Agency). 

The objective of the ITP is to contribute to improved social protection systems to better tackle poverty, vulnerability, inequality (both gender and economic), social exclusion and to contribute to inclusive social development and equitable economic growth. The programme will be implemented in ten to fifteen countries in Africa and Asia, starting in Ethiopia, Kenya, Tanzania, Uganda and Zambia. 

Intended outcomes include:
1) Strengthening government capacity
2) Improving social protection systems/outcomes
3) Building development synergies
4) Rights-based approaches to improve gender equality
5) Strengthening organisational integrity

The core modules of the ITP will include training in six main areas:
 1) Rights-based and life cycle frameworks for social protection systems,
2) The design and implementation of social protection systems to ensure social inclusion,                                                                                                                                                                                                                     3) Strengthening developmental impacts (&quot;Social Protection Plus&quot;1 and the SDGs),                                                                                                                                                                                                                          4) Enabling social protection to promote gender equality, 
5) Financing and co-financing social protection reforms, expansions and integrations, and:
6) Monitoring and evaluating social protection systems to enable evidence-based change. 

In addition, the ITP will innovate specific modules and training components to support the specific change programmes identified by partner country teams.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The objective of the ITP is to contribute to improved social protection systems to better tackle poverty, vulnerability, inequality (both gender and economic) and social exclusion and to contribute to inclusive social development and equitable economic growth. The programme is being implemented during 2019-2024 in ten countries in Africa and Asia (Ethiopia, Kenya, Tanzania, Uganda, Zambia, Rwanda, Mozambique, Zimbabwe, Sudan, and Cambodia).

Intended outcome areas:
1) Strengthening government capacity
2) Improving social protection systems/outcomes
3) Building development synergies
4) Rightsbased approaches to improve gender equality
5) Strengthening organisational integrity 

Central to the ITP are the change programs that each country team develop and implement throughout the implementation period. The change programs are inherited between cohorts of participants in each country, allowing for more long term approaches and focus on sustainability</narrative>
  </description>
